[INTERFACE]
UID: KM271-HWA-021
STATUS: Draft
KIND: Electrical
TITLE: GPIO allocation
DESCRIPTION: Assignment of the ESP32-S3 GPIOs on the v2.0 board.
SIGNALS: >>>
- GPIO0: BOOT (SW3, auto-reset Q1/Q2)
- GPIO2: free (former I2C_EXT_EN)
- GPIO4: ADC1_CH3, 5 V monitor
- GPIO5: VDRV, switchable sensor pull-up supply (via R53, DNP)
- GPIO6/7/8: ADC1_CH5/CH6/CH7, J6 pins 6/4/2
- GPIO9: SCL
- GPIO10: nCS
- GPIO11: MOSI
- GPIO12: SCLK
- GPIO13: MISO
- GPIO14: nINT
- GPIO15: OneWire
- GPIO16: SDA (W5500 reset on the extension)
- GPIO17: KM271 TX (to LM_RX)
- GPIO18: KM271 RX (from LM_TX)
- GPIO19/20: USB D-/D+ (native USB)
- GPIO21: LED D1 green (network)
- GPIO38: LED D2 green (heartbeat)
- GPIO39: LED D3 yellow (Logamatic communication)
- GPIO40: LED D4 red (error)
- GPIO41/42: USER1 (SW2) / USER2 (SW1)
- GPIO43/44: UART0 TXD0/RXD0 (CP2102N, J4)
- EN: RESET (SW4, auto-reset Q1/Q2)
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
GPIO35-37 are unused (octal PSRAM pins on other module variants). GPIO45/46
are strapping pins and left unconnected.
<<<
RELATIONS:
